# Crashing Wave with waterbend {2}: Bot1 taps Memnite and Ornithopter to pay it (CR 701.67a), and taps Bot2's Grizzly Bears and Phyrexian Walker (up to X = 2 targets).
# Then (CR 608.2c) the three stun counters are distributed, one at a time, among the tapped creatures Bot2 controls: two on the Bears, one on the Walker.
# Bot1's own tapped Memnite and Ornithopter are no choice, and neither is Bot2's untapped Llanowar Elves. The pool is empty after the cast:
# X = 2 took exactly two taps.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Island
Memnite
Ornithopter
Crashing Wave
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Llanowar Elves
Grizzly Bears
Phyrexian Walker
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Phyrexian Walker.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Crashing Wave.Cast(X: 2; Convoke: Memnite, Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears; Bot2.Battlefield.Phyrexian Walker)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Choose(Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Choose(Phyrexian Walker)
? Bot1.Mana =
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Counters.Stun = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Phyrexian Walker.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Phyrexian Walker.Counters.Stun = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Counters.Stun = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Counters.Stun = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Stun = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Crashing Wave
